  "dmNarration": [
    "The trail ends below a wooded hill. A shallow stream runs from a dark cave mouth, with a narrow path beside it. Briars crowd the bank. Cold water murmurs over stone.",
    "The stream and the strip of dry ground offer different approaches to the same black opening. From outside, you can study the banks and the briars before stepping beneath the hill; the sound of running water makes the darkness beyond seem deeper."
  ],
  "question": "The party chose to conceal and secure the wagon and all travel together; its risk is recorded. Inspection traced the snare cord to a bent sapling, and Mage Hand exposed the pit edge. You tested firm ground around both hazards and crossed individually. After the cautious five-mile walk, the stream leads to this cave. The guide remains disarmed and watched. How do you approach and what lights your path?",
